{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The three core artifacts are all this trip and nothing on them conflicts: trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown each carry TRP-00307; the trace first and last fixes are 18:01:17 and 18:31:17 and the trip_record's started_at and ended_at are 18:01:17 and 18:31:17, so no timestamp runs backwards and the rider discharges the initial burden in POL-RD-08(a) on a matching trip identifier and consistent pickup-side timestamps.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00307", "EV-GPS-00307", "EV-FARE-00307"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.39
    },
    {
      "text": "Measured on the field POL-RD-01 makes governing, the excess clears both limbs of the threshold. gps_trace.trace_distance_km is 22.6 against an optimal_distance_km of 18.0, an excess of 4.6 km and 25.56%: greater than 20% and greater than 0.8 km, so the threshold is met. trip_record.actual_distance_km shows the same 22.6 km but POL-RD-01 expressly forbids citing that rounded convenience copy for the threshold test, so the rider does not rely on it. Full disclosure under POL-GEN-02(1): EV-GPS-00307 carries weight 0.39 with issue codes GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW and LOW_COVERAGE.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00307", "EV-TRIP-00307"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 0.39
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace is impaired for POLICY purposes and not merely in the schema pre-pass: it carries one gap of 240 seconds, from 18:16:17 to 18:20:17, sitting inside the KPE stretch this rider disputes, and 240 seconds is well over the 90 second limit in POL-RD-07(a). The rider states the impairment openly rather than presenting the trace as clean: EV-GPS-00307 is at weight 0.39 with issue codes GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW and LOW_COVERAGE, and on this trip the two tests coincide — schema-impaired and policy-impaired.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00307"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "gaps[0].duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 0.39
    },
    {
      "text": "No independent corroboration of the excess exists anywhere in this bundle, so POL-RD-07(ii) bars establishing the deviation on the gps_trace alone: the chat log holds zero messages and therefore no driver admission, the fare_breakdown's erp_gantries list is empty with tolls_erp at 0.00 so no charged gantry places the vehicle on a corridor the optimal route does not use, the driver's counterparty statement denies the detour instead of admitting the route, and trip_record.actual_distance_km is the identical 22.6 km figure that POL-RD-01 itself calls a rounded convenience copy of the same trace measurement, not an independent derivation.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00307", "EV-FARE-00307", "EV-TRIP-00307", "EV-GPS-00307"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.39
    },
    {
      "text": "The consequence the policy prescribes is escalation, and escalation is the disposition that protects this rider. POL-RD-07(iii) says that where an impaired trace has no independent corroboration the claim is not sustained on the present record and the outcome is ESCALATE rather than NO_ACTION, because the absence of proof is a data failure and not a finding for the driver; POL-RD-10(3) makes that escalation mandatory. Under POL-GEN-03 NO_ACTION is party-relative and would leave the present state standing, and the fare here is payment_status CHARGED with refund_issued_sgd 0.00, so NO_ACTION would leave the 29.95 charge in place, whereas an escalated amount is held rather than collected.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00307", "EV-GPS-00307"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-10", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.payment_status",
      "asserted_weight": 0.39
    },
    {
      "text": "Escalation is independently compelled by the confidence arithmetic. The only artifact carrying the measured excess is EV-GPS-00307, and under POL-GEN-02(2) confidence may not exceed the weight_multiplier of the artifact that carries the deciding fact, so it is capped at 0.39 — below the platform-wide 0.70 floor, which fires POL-RD-10(1). The bundle_integrity_score is context and not the cap, and because the second candidate carrier (trip_record.actual_distance_km) is a copy of the same measurement rather than an independent one, the maximum-of-two-carriers rule does not lift the cap.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00307", "EV-TRIP-00307"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-02", "POL-RD-10"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.39
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's explanation takes him nowhere. 'KPE straight down, no exit. GPS always drops in the tunnel' names no road or segment, cites no evidence ID and invokes no clause. The traffic advisory for this trip is absent from the bundle — EV-ADVIS-00307-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0, and its absence is itself citable — so POL-RD-03 cannot be run at all: with no advisory covering the window there is nothing to compare against the optimal corridor, and the driver's assertion is an uncited excuse that POL-RD-08 discards. Under POL-RD-13 an assertion tested against an absent advisory neither reduces the measured excess nor supplies an amended optimal route.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00307-01", "EV-CHAT-00307", "EV-GPS-00307"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-13", "POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.39
    },
    {
      "text": "The disputed overrun is not an artefact of the outage, which is why the amount should be held rather than left collected. Under POL-RD-07(i) the whole distance across the impaired stretch is bounded, at most favourably to the driver, by the 3.01 km straight line between the bounding fixes, yet the total excess is 4.6 km; the excess therefore cannot be located wholly inside the gap, and at least 1.59 km of it falls on sampled track outside the outage. The rider is not asking the tribunal to guess what happened inside the tunnel — the rider's point is that the billed distance exceeds the optimal route by more than the tunnel can explain.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00307", "EV-TRIP-00307"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 0.39
    },
    {
      "text": "If the tribunal is nonetheless able to decide the merits rather than escalate, the refund is arithmetic and runs the rider's way. The trip is METERED so POL-RD-02 applies and POL-RD-11 does not; the surge multiplier read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier is 1.0; recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 x 18.0 + 0.28 x 24.0) x 1.0 + 0.80 platform fee = 24.82 against a charged_total of 29.95, a refund of 5.1300 rounded up to 5.15. That is above the 0.50 de minimis and is 17.13% of charged_total, so it is a PARTIAL_REFUND and the 90% full-refund share in POL-RD-02 is not reached. No ERP or toll line exists (0.00), so nothing is added on top of the POL-RD-02 figure.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00307", "EV-TRIP-00307", "EV-GPS-00307"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-RD-11", "POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.payable",
      "asserted_weight": 0.39
    },
    {
      "text": "This rider is not the serial claimant POL-RD-08 guards against, so no additional corroboration burden attaches to the claim: rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 0 and deviation_claims_60d_substantiated is 0, so the four-or-more-claims with one-or-fewer-substantiated condition is not met on this record and that factor may not be used to deny a claim that is otherwise proven.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-00307"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

