    "explanation": "Both parties: this case cannot be decided on the present record, and it is being sent to a human reviewer. No money moves here — the SGD 29.95 charge is held, not collected and not refunded, until that review.\n\nWHY IT ESCALATES. The GPS trace for trip TRP-00307 (EV-GPS-00307) is impaired. It carries a single 240-second gap between consecutive fixes, from 18:16:17 to 18:20:17, inside the KPE tunnel stretch that is the subject of the dispute, with coverage of 86.7% across the 1,800-second active window. That is a policy-level impairment under POL-RD-07(a), not merely a schema flag, and the artifact is carried at weight 0.39 with issue codes GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW and LOW_COVERAGE.\n\nBecause the trace is impaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c), POL-RD-07(ii) forbids establishing a deviation on the trace alone. I have checked each of the four independent sources it names and none is on this bundle. The chat log (EV-CHAT-00307) holds 0 messages, so there is no driver admission and no rider instruction. The fare breakdown (EV-FARE-00307) shows an empty erp_gantries set and SGD 0.00 of tolls, so no charged gantry places the vehicle on a corridor the optimal route does not use. The driver's own counterparty statement denies the detour rather than admitting the route. And trip_record.actual_distance_km (22.6 km) is, in POL-RD-01's own words, a rounded convenience copy of the same trace measurement, so it is not an independent derivation. Under POL-RD-07(iii) the claim is therefore not sustained on this record and the outcome is ESCALATE rather than NO_ACTION, because what has failed is the data and not the driver. POL-RD-10(3) makes that escalation mandatory.\n\nThe confidence arithmetic points the same way. The measured excess is carried by EV-GPS-00307 alone at weight 0.39, and the trip_record figure is a copy of that same measurement rather than a second, independent carrier, so POL-GEN-02(2) caps confidence at 0.39 — below the platform-wide 0.70 floor — which fires POL-RD-10(1) as well. (bundle_integrity_score is context for the reader, not the cap.)\n\nTHE CLAIMS THAT SURVIVED. The rider's arithmetic is correct as far as it goes: on the trace figure of 22.6 km against an optimal of 18.0 km the excess is 4.6 km and 25.56%, clearing both limbs of POL-RD-01 (over 0.8 km and over 20%); and had the trace been clean, the POL-RD-02 refund would be charged_total 29.95 less a recomputed fare of 24.82 — that is 5.13, rounded up to 5.15, about 17.1% of the charge, a partial refund and nowhere near the 90% full-refund share. But that computation runs on the impaired trace alone, which is exactly what POL-RD-07(ii) forbids. The driver's points are answered too: no repeat pattern is established (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 260 completed trips in 90 days, falling short of POL-RD-06), so neither the POL-RD-06(b) uplift nor a POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral arises; and the derived speed profile across the sampled fixes (43.5 to 46.9 kph, with no stationary fix) is consistent with continuous expressway running, though POL-RD-07(i) reads the impaired stretch as the 3.01 km straight line between its bounding fixes in any event. The driver's traffic explanation ('KPE straight down, no exit') names no road and cites no evidence, and the traffic advisory for this trip (EV-ADVIS-00307-01) is MISSING at weight 0.0, so POL-RD-03 cannot be run and the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08; but under POL-RD-13 that changes nothing here, because where the trace itself is impaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c) with no corroboration, POL-RD-10(3) still governs.\n\nNo referral fires. POL-RD-06(c) needs an established repeat pattern and there is none; POL-RD-09(4) has no unmatched charge line to attach to, the ERP and toll total being 0.00.\n\nWHAT WOULD RESOLVE IT. The reviewer needs an independent record from inside the 240-second gap: a GPS export from a second device, an ERP gantry record with gantry name, entry time and cashcard statement placing the vehicle on or off the optimal corridor, a call log, or a contemporaneous photograph with its capture time."
